839] \"Love of Three Oranges is a masterpiece written by Soviet composer Prokofiev during his escape. He was not yet thirty years old at the time, and this work, along with 'Lieutenant Kije,' has become his signature piece.\" [840] \"I've only heard of 'Peter and the Wolf.'\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 6:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:46:28 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nWhen Ito's head was cut off, the brain cells were temporarily paralyzed due to the low temperature. When the neural fibers of Utsugi were combined with them, the temperature difference between the neural fibers caused the production of an electromotive force. This electromotive force became the electric potential for neural activity, which activated the retracting nerves in a state of apparent death. In other words, Ito's nerves and Utsugi's nerves were indeed connected. [3969] \"Now, let's talk about muscles. Modern medicine shows that muscles can be repaired, and muscles that have just been cut and have not yet oxidized can be connected together. Although they cannot make large movements, they can still temporarily remain connected due to their adhesiveness. [3970] \"Connecting a person who has died once?\" [3971] \"No, strictly speaking, Itou has not yet died. I'm not sure what the death criteria for humans are, but even brain death cannot occur in less than zero point zero one seconds. Yes, the head and body cut off are still alive. As for whether it can be called the first death, this question should be considered by the gods. [3972] \"However, this anomaly created a monster with Utsugi's body - Dr. Frankenstein. At this moment, the blood vessels and trachea are not important. This artificial person only needs to survive for a short time. [3973] \"A short time?\" The chief inspector asked. [3974] \"Yes, because Itou only needs a few minutes. Now I will explain the significance of this. [3975] \"Mutsu took a deep breath and showed a hesitant expression on his face.\" [3976] \"In short, It\u00f4 received a new body from Utsunomiya and opened his eyes again due to this shock. Of course, the most surprised person was Maki. She thought she had killed someone - and even switched bodies - and suddenly opened her eyes and stood up. [3977] \"This is a horror movie. I can't believe it. [3978] \"So, what did It\u00f4 see when he woke up due to the hand of the gods? Yes, what he saw was Maki, who was standing there holding a knife. And It\u00f4 remembered. His memories at the moment of death - he woke up from a coma due to the shock of having his head cut off, and now he saw himself about to be killed. [3979] \"Due to extreme fear, It\u00f4 ran out of the room, desperately trying to escape into the 'Gate of Hell.' He grabbed the key that was placed beside him. Yes, we thought Utsunomiya had escaped into the Gate of Hell, which is why it felt unnatural. But if we think that It\u00f4 ran into the Gate of Hell to escape, it makes perfect sense. After all, Utsunomiya's body was being controlled by It\u00f4's consciousness. [3980] \"Of course, It\u00f4 probably wanted to cry for help. But it was like someone whose throat had been cut, who could only make a horrible, gurgling sound. At that time, it was unclear to what extent It\u00f4's consciousness was awake, but he instinctively fled to the 'Gate of Hell.' Then, when It\u00f4 reached the 'Gate of Hell,' he naturally locked it from the inside. [3981] \"His body belonged to Ushio, but his head - his spirit belonged to Itou. Itou is left-handed, so he locked the door with his left hand as usual. That's why the left hand of the right-handed Ushio spasmed due to the abrupt twisting movement he was not used to.\" [3982] \"However, at this point, Itou was already exhausted. Although the nerve fibers were connected, a person whose muscles and blood vessels were cut off could not live long. After Itou locked the door, he fell down naturally, holding the key with his left hand.\" [3983] \"This is the reason why Ushio's left hand was holding the key.\" [3984] \"When Itou fell down, the head separated from Ushio's body and became a mere head and corpse. As life stopped, blood flowed out, creating the illusion that the 'Gate of Hell' was the scene of the crime.\" [3985] \"This is the solution to the locked room. The 'Gate of Hell' is a complete locked room. As for the locksmith, I have no intention of hiding it. It was the hand of the god.\" [3986] The police chief still looked incredulous. I was the same. No, I didn't want to believe it. It was too terrifying. However, Kumozawa said it was divine behavior. [3987] \"But it's a fact,\" Kumozawa emphasized repeatedly with a serious tone. [3988] \"So, what did Mutsuki do after that? \" [3989] \"At this point, an ordinary murderer would have been frightened and abandoned all plans, but Mutsuki was a genius, no, a madman. He took advantage of this incredible situation. [3990] \"Now, let's recall the items in Haya's room. There were things that showed Haya's characteristics: the racehorse named Reindeer, and the LP record.\" [3991] \"In fact, I was misled by the title of that record. The intended theme was 'America,' but my attention was drawn to 'Death and the Maiden,' which was full of suggestive and seductive elements. Of course, this also fully reflected the killer's intentions. [3992] \"You should understand now. Ueda's room was meant to suggest 'The American Gun Mystery.' Mistuho originally planned to use the horse and the record as props to show this. [3993] \"By coincidence, Ueda (It\u00f4) created a locked room himself. [3994] \"When Mistuho realized that 'Hell's Gate' had become a locked room, she improvised and abandoned the 'American Gun Mystery' idea, replacing it with 'The Chinese Orange Mystery,' which was the only one that focused on the locked room. [3995] \"Mistuho returned to the dining room and brought an orange. She probably