o the strong impression caused by the Ito-Uma murder case, we overestimated the killer and thought that the killer would not easily leave clues. This was my mistake. [4008] \"But, Mizutani didn't take anything with her hands at that time, did she?\" [4009] I remember that Mounta had testified to this. [4010] \"She put them in her skirt. She wrapped them in a bag before putting them in. It is said that there were many such pickpocket gangs in America around ten years ago. They even stole medium-sized televisions, but the principle is the same. To an outsider, it looks like they didn't take anything.\" [4011] \"Akiba used this trick out of caution, which brought her good luck. As a result, her cautious adventure made her even further away from the circle of suspects. [4012] \"There is nothing remarkable afterwards. The initial murder took a lot of effort, no, the secret room was also purely accidental, and she chose a safe method afterwards. She was afraid that too much refinement would put her in danger. [4013] \"When killing Jouma, she held up the head of Tamekichi in the corridor. She wore a larger size of clothes and placed Tamekichi's head on her own head. There is a similar scene in the recently discovered tragedy of Aeschylus. I don't know if Akiba referred to it. Then, she made Yuzu see this scene, thus luring me to open Tamekichi's coffin. [4014] \"Wakaba and Kanae, as well as Jouma's murder, were almost untouched except for decapitation. [4015] \"In addition, discovering Hikari was a stroke of luck for Akiba. Otherwise, it would have been a great loss for her face.\" [4016] \"But there's Yuzuha too, right?\" [4017] \"No,\" Wakisugi denied, \"Yuzuha was part of Fujiko's murder plan from the beginning. However, Yuzuha was also lucky. Because just in the nick of time, Tomioka's relative, McArthur, appeared. [4018] \"Fujiko has only been in Japan for five months, and I don't think she knows McArthur's true identity. Moreover, it would be dangerous to ask someone else to investigate, and it's probably impossible. McArthur must have contacted her after coming here. [4019] I remember McArthur saying he was going to Fujiko's room that night. Maybe Fujiko found out about it then. [4020] \"McArthur must have discovered the truth before us. So, he planned to team up with Fujiko. He revealed his identity as Tomioka's son and prepared to take Tomioka's property with Fujiko.\" [4021] \"However, Mistuho's goal was different from his. McArthur didn't realize his mistake and believed that Mistuho also aimed for the property. [4022] \"Meanwhile, Mistuho revised the plan, hastily removed Y\u016ben, who had no blood ties, from the list, and killed McArthur instead. At this point, the choice of theme was simple. Since he was wearing a top hat, there was only one possible theme: 'The Mystery of the Roman Hat.' [4023] \"By the way, Y\u016ben always wore a lace cap, so she would have been killed using the theme of 'The Mystery of the Roman Hat' originally.\" [4024] So, if it wasn't for McArthur, the head on the table would have been Y\u016ben's with a lace cap on, right? [4025] \"Suguru was left for 'The Mystery of the Egyptian Cross,' so Y\u016ben's 'The Mystery of the American Gun' was also decided. As you can see, Mistuho's plan was flexible and adaptable, allowing her to achieve the best outcome from all situations.\" [4026] \"Mr. McCarto's reasoning yesterday was probably nonsense. Since he had teamed up with the fog drawing, he had to come up with a suitable answer. He said so, didn't he? Because I'm the killer, I have to leave this house to avoid getting too involved. [4027] \"However, this was actually about Mr. McCarto himself. It was Mr. McCarto who got too involved. Even after his mother was killed, he still cooperated with the fog drawing. As a result, he ended up losing his life. [4028] \"I thought of Akutagawa's 'Tsuchigumo'. Tsuchigumo couldn't bear to see his parents suffering in hell and shouted out loud. Unexpectedly, Tsuchigumo was saved by this action. However, Mr. McCarto watched his mother being killed - even though he didn't know about it beforehand - and took on the guilt himself. [4029] \"It's more like the story in 'The Spider Silk', isn't it? [4030] \"Why did the fog drawing do this?\" The detective murmured dejectedly.\" [4031] \"The motive... it's a twisted Oedipus complex.\" [4032] Wakisugi pointed to the shining corpse of Kanayan with his right hand. [4033] \"What does it look like?\" [4034] Wakisugi, who questioned like a rhetorician, was ultimately a failure. [4035] He gave the answer himself. [4036] \"It's a 'god.' The only savior who descended to this world\u2026\n[4037] \"This is what Fujiko truly pursued. She loved her father Kanayanagi. She didn't hate the Kanayanagi who abandoned her and her mother, but instead constantly missed him from afar in a distant foreign land. It's probably the influence of her mother, who was deeply in love with Kanayanagi, that led her to believe he was her savior.\" [4038] \"Kanayanagi?\" [4039] \"Yes. But reality is different. The Kanayanagi who came to meet Fujiko was just a weak and powerless ordinary citizen. Recognizing this, Fujiko's disappointment must have been immeasurable. After twenty years of accumulated expectations, this tragic fact was equivalent to the collapse of her value system and her desire for redemption. [4040] \"In a normal situation, Fujiko would have given up her illusions about Kanayanagi\u2014no, her faith. But she pursued something else. She pursued 'god.' And she inherited the bloodline of the Mimura family.\" [4041] \"Mistuho would do anything to make Kaji into 'God'. If the reality of him was too disappointing, she would create a new 'God' herself. A new Christ\u2026\"\n[4042] \"\u2026\"\n[4043] \"At this point, Mistuho changed her role from a humble believer like Peter to the Virgin Mary. In order to make Kaji into 'God', she had to eliminate other members of the Mikumo family, making him the only 'God' and giving him all the power of the Mikumo family. With both 'blood' and 'power', the great father Kaji that Mistuho envisioned could be born. [4044] \"She was insane. But she held onto the lofty ideals of a fanatical believer and charged towards her own peak. She created her own aesthetics and overcame all obstacles. [4045] \"And now, Kaji has become 'God'.\" [4046] \"Of course, not the living Kanou. The living Kanou was insignificant. The 'Kanou' filled with Mistuho's ideas had to be a mere collection of facts, an entity beyond all, a god symbolized. [4047] \"Therefore, Kanou must obtain death. This is to obtain eternal brilliance. [4048] \"Immortality\u2026\"\n[4049] \"Yes. In order to live on forever in Mistuho's heart, Kanou must undergo the baptism of death and be purified.\" [4050] \"This is called purification?\" [4051] I looked at Yan. Perhaps due to the stimulation of the words of Muto, the illusion of the golden halo on the cross of Yan came to me. [4052] \"Yes. Now he is no longer the Yan we know, but a 'god'. And when this act ends, the faith of mist-drawn is fulfilled. In this sense, perhaps it is not Yan who is 'catharsis', but mist-drawn.\" [4053] \"Are you saying that mist-drawn committed a murder to purify itself?\" [4054] \"That's the most appropriate way to put it. For mist-drawn, this is a holy war, a suffering.\" [4055] Muto uttered the last sentence. No one was prepared to speak. [4056] The church was enveloped in a heavy atmosphere. [4057] I looked at the organ in the right corner. The image of Fujiko playing the \"Passepied\" came to my mind. What did that scene mean? What was that divine light, that pious prayer of Bach? [4058] For a moment, I couldn't believe it. [4059] Soon, the detective asked, \"So, where is Fujiko now?\" [4060] \"The 'Hell Gate'.\" [4061] A tone of giving up on life. Like Icarus losing his son. [4062] \"Mifune is probably no longer in this world. She ascended to heaven with Kaneko to become the Virgin Mary. The final work of Quine Nation's Ten Mysteries, what is the tenth one?\" [4063] \"The Japanese Thrush Mystery...\"\n[4064] \"What is the ending of the book?\" [4065] \"Suicide... That's it, right?\" [4066] Mukashige nodded calmly. [4067] \"It was her own choice. She gave birth to 'God', so she didn't have to follow God's laws. She completed Quinn's epic narrative poem with her own death. [4068] \"And there is only one way to sever one's head. It exists in the 'Gate of Hell.'\" [4069] \"The guillotine!?\" [4070] The inspector called out, but his voice was weak and feeble. [4071]We entered 'Hell's Gate'. [4072]The scent of blood wafted in the darkness. [4073]Hurai lifted the lamp, dispelling the final darkness. [4074]The guillotine was dragged to the center of the room. The beautiful woman lay on it, her right hand gripping the knife that had taken ten lives.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 7:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:46:28 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nWhat about this one?\" [841] \"Nothing 'what about this one.' I just want to say that the title of the second suite is 'Hellish Scene.'\" [842] For a moment, the detective was stunned and held his forehead with his hand. I also felt that it was a stretch, just like 'Death and the Maiden.' [843] \"But there are more than three orange seeds, and there are more than ten that have fallen. How do you explain that?\" [844] \"I'm still investigating.\" [845] The detective snorted, \"You have a tendency to try to acknowledge the existence of something. This one is no different... You might be right in a millionth of a percent, but I still deny it.\" [846] \"That's how we make progress,\" said Kuroda, smiling. \"Everything is fragmented. There's nothing else that's appeared yet. So I'm just picking up the fragments. Of course, I haven't decided where to put them yet. We have to gather as many fragments as possible.\" [847] \"It might not even be possible to put them together,\" the detective responded sarcastically. [848] \"That's true. But it can't hurt to keep an eye on the oranges, can it?\" [849] \"It depends on whether hell appears as you say.\" [850] \"Well, hell has already appeared. The next ones to come will be the prince and princess.\" [851] At that moment, a knock sounded from outside. [852] \"Sorry,\" said Nakamura, the detective who had rushed up the stairs red-faced when the horse's head was found. \"This is a report from the forensic department.\" [853] Without saying a word, Nakamura flipped through the report in his hand, likely an impatient person. [854] \"The victim's head and body match. The feet also fit. It is estimated that Ito died between 3:00 a.m. and 3:30 a.m. The same goes for the horse.\" [855] \"Shortened to thirty minutes, huh? Anyway, it doesn't matter. So what else?\" urged Jingu. The inspector seemed to dislike overly formal reports. [856] \"As for the cause of death, it was not poison. No trace of drug poisoning was found. Both of them were...\"\n[857] \"What's wrong?\" [858] \"Ah, I'm sorry. The cause of death is the severance of the spinal cord. It says they died on the spot.\" [859] \"Neck cord...\" Mochizuki murmured, as if chewing on the meaning of the words. [860] \"So...both of them were killed by decapitation?\" [861] The police chief grunted, a shudder of horror passing through him. This was different from the previous astonishment. The killer had not severed the victims' heads from their bodies but had cut them off while they were still alive. The victims' screams had been replaced by the cries of the living. Both Ito and Umino had been sent to the guillotine alive. [862] \"Yes, that's what it seems like. There was a live reaction detected on the cut surface.\" [863] \"What a mess!\" Tsujimura clutched his white hair. \"Maybe we're dealing with not just a high-class criminal, but a real monster \u2013 the worst kind!\" [864] \"It's like a demon,\" Kumotsuma said, rare praise on his lips. His expression didn't reveal whether he was shaken or not. \"And who this head is for is also a question.\" [865] \"Is it possible that the feet were also cut off before they died?\" The police chief ignored Kumotsuma's words and asked. [866] \"No, Ito's two feet were cut off after death, about thirty minutes later, they said.\" [867] I felt a little relieved. If Ito's feet were cut off while still alive...just thinking about it made me shudder. Horikawa seemed to have the same feeling, as his lips twitched slightly earlier, and his extreme tension seemed to have eased a little. [868] \"What about the weapon?\" [869] \"The details are not clear yet. They said it was severed with a sharp blade in one go.\" [870] If it were a meat cleaver or an axe, the cut would be very rough, as it requires skill. However, both Ito and Uma's necks were very flat, like slices of radish or cucumber. The only weapon the killer could have used was a knife that had been tempered a thousand times for beheading. [871] \"In one stroke... It's almost like a beheading expert. Does the killer have experience in this?\" [872] Nakamura hesitated as he quickly scanned the report. [873] \"No. Ito and Uma's backs of the head had bruises, so they were probably knocked unconscious before their heads were cut off. At that time, it is said that even an amateur could use a heavy knife like a chopper to cut off the head with the momentum of the knife itself.\" [874] This statement couldn't help but remind me of a Chinese hero who wielded the Dragon Blade with ease. Of course, he also had a long beard...\n[875] \"What about the guillotine?\" [876] \"There were no signs of use or bloodstains.\" [877] \"You mean the guillotine has been used before?\" [878] \"Well, it's complicated...\"\n[879] It seems this report didn't take into account Woodside's personal preferences. [880] \"Then it must be the knife.\" [881] \"If it's a big knife, there would be plenty of them i